    "created_at": "2021-02-22T21:12:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-02-22T21:12:30Z",
    "body": "My gut says that adding something that changes background colors for the actual module lines would be problematic for several reasons:\r\n\r\n- It won't actually stretch all the way across the screen (e.g. if your prompt is just `~`, then the background color will be one character wide--we'd have to add some sort of padding module to make it extend the entire line)\r\n- Maintaining this and deciding what happens on color conflict adds a whole bunch of complexity to the prompt that will rarely be tested.\r\n- It's another thing that has to be checked for when adding new modules.\r\n\r\nBut! I do think that there's a way to accomplish this by promoting `add_newline` to a full \"module.\" If we do that, then we can add options to fill character and color (e.g. request background fill on the blank line, or use a bunch of `*   *   *` to separate prompts).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
