    "created_at": "2022-03-22T05:35:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-22T05:35:09Z",
    "body": "What about this?  \r\n\r\n1 - Add a background variable to each module, thus separating it from the style variable.  We could call this `style_bg` or similar.  This would first allow us to easily change the background of the full module output.  This also fixes the current issue of trying to change backgrounds in a module since `style` doesn't apply to the full module output (for instance, in Time style applies to the time but not the ` at `).\r\n\r\n2 - In prompt, also add a `bg_override` variable that can override the background of all modules specified in the prompt?  This would still allow us to use `(bg:???)` in the prompt format for characters that we may not want to share that background, such as prompts.  \r\n\r\nThis will allow a full line color change as initially requested in this thread using `Fill` and also help people create powerline10k like prompts much more easily rather than the current requirement of having to literally redo EVERY format and style variable of every module.\r\n\r\nAs a side note, grouping modules that logically flow together (like all the Github ones) into super modules or some-such, then creating a universal separator that applies between super modules would be the final element to make powerline10k fonts easy to re-create in Starship.\r\n\r\nSorry if these suggestions fit in a different issue thread.",
