    "body": "Well, if anyone's really desperate for this feature, I made an **extremely hacky** workaround (for zsh):\r\n\r\n```\r\nPS1=\"%K{black}${PS1%)}\"' | sed -E -e '\"'\"'s#%\\{\\x1b\\[0m%\\}#\\0%K\\{black\\}#g'\"'\"' -e '\"'\"'$ ! {/.{'\"'\"'\"$COLUMNS\"'\"'\"'}/!{s#$#'\"'\"'\"${(l:COLUMNS:: :)SPACE}\"'\"'\"'#;s#^(((%.?\\{[^\\}]*\\})*.){'\"'\"'\"$COLUMNS\"'\"'\"'}).*#\\1#}}'\"'\"')'\r\nbgcolor_reset() { echo -n '\\e[0m' }\r\npreexec_functions+=(bgcolor_reset)\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt replaces all the reset color ansi codes with reset color and then set background to black (that's the `%K{black}` parts), and also pads the output lines with spaces so that the changed colour reaches to the end of line.",
